# Requests for the Visual Studio / VS Code REST client.
# 1. Run "Sign in" and copy accessToken into @token.
# 2. Try the other requests with different demo users to see 401, 403 and 404 responses.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-access-token-here

### Sign in (demo password for every user: Passw0rd!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "accountant@contoso.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### My profile and effective permissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List invoices (needs invoices.view)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a draft invoice (needs invoices.create)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Fourth Coffee",
  "amount": 450.00
}

### Export (needs invoices.view AND invoices.export)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Roles (needs roles.view) - try with admin@contoso.test
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Permission catalogue (needs roles.view)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices
